{
  "comment": "What counts as a URL property value, shared by src/lib/url-value.ts (urlHref) and src-tauri/src/url_value.rs (href): the schemes of shared/external-protocols.json (an authority scheme needs a non-empty host after //, a mail scheme needs local@domain), or a bare domain (dot-separated ASCII labels, a TLD of 2+ letters, optional port, path, query or fragment) which opens as https. No whitespace or control character anywhere; any other scheme (javascript:, ftp:, file:) is refused. Both tests read this file; href is the address handed to the system browser. A bare `name.ext` whose extension is a vault file's (the union of shared/attachments.json importExtensions and renderExtensions, shared/code-files.json neverExtensions and shared/vault-file-extensions.json) is a file name, not a domain; with a path, a scheme or www. it is still a URL.",
